IMPORT prelude

-- Civil Law (Wrongs) Act 2002 (ACT) -- the dates, in one small module.
--
-- It uses only the built-in date functions (DATE_FROM_DMY, DATE_SERIAL, DATE_FROM_SERIAL, DATE_DAY, DATE_MONTH,
-- DATE_YEAR), not the daydate library. Dates are compared by serial.
--
-- "Within 1 month after the day X" and "the day that is 9 months after X" are read with the day X excluded and the
-- period ending on the corresponding day of the later month, or on the last day of that month if it has no
-- corresponding day (31 January + 1 month = 28 or 29 February). The Legislation Act 2001 (ACT), which says how ACT
-- periods are counted (ss 151-151C), is not deposited: this reading is fork F2 in NOTES.md. A last day on a weekend or
-- public holiday is NOT moved: ACT public holidays are not deposited.
--
-- (c) Australian Capital Territory. Used under CC BY 4.0 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md). Unofficial text.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Dates for the Civil Law (Wrongs) Act 2002`

GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the calendar date` d m y MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY d m y

-- Plain days from one day to another (negative if the second is earlier).
GIVEN `the start` IS A DATE, `the end` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days from` `the start` `to` `the end` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `the end` MINUS DATE_SERIAL `the start`

-- The day a given number of plain days after a day.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `the start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the date` n `days after` `the start` MEANS DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL `the start` PLUS n)

GIVEN a IS A DATE, b IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the day` a `is after` b IF DATE_SERIAL a GREATER THAN DATE_SERIAL b

GIVEN a IS A DATE, b IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the day` a `is on or before` b IF DATE_SERIAL a AT MOST DATE_SERIAL b

GIVEN a IS A DATE, b IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the later of` a `and` b MEANS
    IF DATE_SERIAL a AT LEAST DATE_SERIAL b
    THEN a
    ELSE b

GIVEN a IS A DATE, b IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the earlier of` a `and` b MEANS
    IF DATE_SERIAL a AT MOST DATE_SERIAL b
    THEN a
    ELSE b

-- The number of days in a calendar month (the first of the next month, less the first of this month).
GIVEN m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the length of month` m `of` y MEANS
    IF m EQUALS 12
    THEN 31
    ELSE DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 (m PLUS 1) y) MINUS DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 m y)

-- The day that is n whole calendar months (n from 1 to 12) after a day: the corresponding day of the month n months on,
-- or the last day of that month if it is shorter (fork F2).
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `the day of the event` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day` n `months after` `the day of the event` MEANS
    IF `the day number` AT MOST `the length of month` `the target month` `of` `the target year`
    THEN DATE_FROM_DMY `the day number` `the target month` `the target year`
    ELSE DATE_FROM_DMY (`the length of month` `the target month` `of` `the target year`) `the target month` `the target year`
    WHERE
        `the day number` MEANS DATE_DAY `the day of the event`
        `the month count` MEANS DATE_MONTH `the day of the event` PLUS n
        `the target month` MEANS
            IF `the month count` GREATER THAN 12
            THEN `the month count` MINUS 12
            ELSE `the month count`
        `the target year` MEANS
            IF `the month count` GREATER THAN 12
            THEN DATE_YEAR `the day of the event` PLUS 1
            ELSE DATE_YEAR `the day of the event`
